<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Daehan Flour buys 21,000T of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Daehan Flour buys 21,000T of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Daehan Flour Mills Co Ltd bought on Wednesday 21,000 tonnes of U.S. No.1 wheat from Japanese trading house Mitsui and Company Ltd, a company official said.  </p>
<p>The official said the 21,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat would be split into four lots -- 3,700 tonnes of western white/soft white wheat, 1,000 tonnes of western white club wheat, 5,000 tonnes of hard red winter wheat (protein minimum 11.5 percent), and 11,300 tonnes of dark northern spring wheat (protein minimum 14 percent).</p>
<p>Shipment was set for August 20-September 20 to the western port of Inchon.</p>
<p>Details for the results are as follow:</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat		   Tonne	Price/T (FOB)</p>
<p>  Western White/Soft White    3,700	 $140.40</p>
<p>  Western White Club Wheat    1,000	 $141.90</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter		 5,000	 $146.80</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring	 11,300	 $171.50</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
